From 134e5beaffabc246c06f89d70f5469856eb107bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:09:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: sizes of the tested functions read in the
 reference library

The comparison program reads the sizes of the variables of a point in the
symbols exported by the library generated by the `generic` interface:
types of the variables, tangent operator blocks, elastic material
properties added when the stiffness tensor is required, and options of
the standard finite strain behaviours. The tested function (integration,
initialize function, post-processing, rotation) and the number of its
inputs or outputs are deduced from its name. The material properties, the
amplitude of the gradients and the temperature are given by options with
default values.

The list of comparisons no longer repeats the sizes of each behaviour,
and the rotations no longer need dummy arguments. The sizes read for the
75 comparisons were checked against the sizes previously given.
---
 .../generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.md   |   5 +-
 .../generic-parallel/compare-all.sh           | 193 ++++----
 .../generic-parallel/compare-functions.sh     |   8 +-
 .../generic-parallel/compare-tdls.sh          |   4 +-
 .../behaviours/generic-parallel/compare.cxx   | 430 ++++++++++++++----
 .../sycl-default-acpp-omp/test.check          |   8 +-
 .../sycl-default-acpp/test.check              |   8 +-
 .../sycl-default-icpx/test.check              |   8 +-
 8 files changed, 465 insertions(+), 199 deletions(-)

